{'symbol': 'VIAC', 'date': '2019-10-28 22:30:00', 'title': 'CBS to Delist Class A and Class B Common Stock from NYSE', 'text': 'CBS Corporation and Viacom Inc. announced that the registration statement on Form S-4 (No. 333-234238) (the “Registration Statement”) filed by CBS with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission was declared effective by the SEC on October 25, 2019. The Registration Statement was filed in connection with the proposed combination of CBS and Viacom and includes a joint consent solicitation statement/prospectus of CBS and Viacom. The companies also announced that their pending merger and the related proposals have been approved by National Amusements Inc. and its affiliate, which satisfies the closing conditions to the merger requiring approval of a majority of the CBS Class A shares and a majority of the Viacom Class A shares. The final results of the consent solicitations of CBS and Viacom will be set forth in the companies’ separate Current Reports on Form 8-K that will be filed with the SEC. The completion of the merger remains subject to other customary closing conditions and is now expected to close by early December 2019. At closing, CBS will be renamed “ViacomCBS Inc.”. In addition, at closing, CBS will delist its Class A and Class B common stock from NYSE and will list ViacomCBS Class A and Class B common stock, including the outstanding shares of CBS Class A and Class B common stock (which will remain outstanding shares of ViacomCBS), on The NASDAQ Stock Market under the new ticker symbols “VIACA” and “VIAC,” respectively.'}
{'symbol': 'V', 'date': '2019-10-28 22:30:00', 'title': 'Visa and Marqeta Offer Fintechs a Path to Growth in Growing Digital Payments Landscape', 'text': 'Visa announced a platform collaboration intended to ease global expansion for multi-national card programs. The project plans to provide a streamlined developer-friendly path for Visa issuers to build, test and launch digital-first card programs in 10 Asia Pacific markets. Asia Pacific is home to 4.3 billion people, and with digital payments expected to increase in the region by $23 trillion over the next decade2. Working with Marqeta and Visa, partners can open a laptop to access Marqeta’s existing sand-box and publicly available APIs. Brands that enter into a commercial partnership with Visa can create new issuing programs and can rapidly build and test consumer payment applications in multiple Asia Pacific markets on the Marqeta platform. Visa and Marqeta’s combined offering is designed to provide a solution for innovators to benefit from the following: Rapidly build new payment applications: Developers will be able to begin testing products in Marqeta’s live sandbox. Test and learn UI/UX: The solution is intended to allow partners to work on the user interface and experience to trial all kinds of creative payment solutions, while also working with the Marqeta issuing API and developer sandbox to set up payment processing. Simplify and accelerate international expansion: The solution is designed to enablepartners to go live across multiple Asia Pacific markets quickly, prioritizing speed, streamlining the burden of launching and scaling new card programs.'}
{'symbol': 'VNO', 'date': '2019-10-28 22:30:00', 'title': 'Vornado Realty Trust Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Vornado Realty Trust announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced total revenue was USD 465.961 million compared to USD 542.048 million a year ago. Net income was USD 335.438 million compared to USD 203.179 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 1.69 compared to USD 1 a year ago. For the nine months, total revenue was USD 1,463.732 million compared to USD 1,620.303 million a year ago. Net income was USD 2,942.187 million compared to USD 336.927 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 15.22 compared to USD 1.5 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 15.2 compared to USD 1.49 a year ago.'}
{'symbol': 'WBA', 'date': '2019-10-28 09:30:00', 'title': 'Walgreens Boots Alliance Reports Q4 Adjusted Earnings Per Share $1.43', 'text': 'WALGREENS BOOTS ALLIANCE REPORTS FISCAL YEAR 2019 RESULTS IN LINE WITH GUIDANCE.Q4 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.43.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.75.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.41 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY SALES INCREASED 1.5 PERCENT TO $34.0 BILLION.WALGREENS BOOTS ALLIANCE - INTRODUCED GUIDANCE OF ROUGHLY FLAT GROWTH IN 2020 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE AT CONSTANT CURRENCY RATES, WITH A RANGE OF PLUS OR MINUS 3%.COMPANY RAISED ITS ANNUAL COST SAVINGS TARGET FROM IN EXCESS OF $1.5 BILLION TO IN EXCESS OF $1.8 BILLION BY FISCAL 2022.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $5.96 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q4 REVENUE VIEW $33.89 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.RETAIL PHARMACY USA HAD Q4 SALES OF $26.0 BILLION, AN INCREASE OF 2.1 PERCENT OVER YEAR-AGO QUARTER.RETAIL PHARMACY INTERNATIONAL HAD Q4 SALES OF $2.7 BILLION, A DECREASE OF 6.3 PERCENT FROM YEAR-AGO QUARTER.QTRLY RETAIL PHARMACY USA SALES IN COMPARABLE STORES INCREASED 3.4 PERCENT.QTRLY RETAIL PHARMACY INTERNATIONAL COMPARABLE PHARMACY SALES DECREASED 1.0 PERCENT ON A CONSTANT CURRENCY BASIS.FOR RETAIL PHARMACY USA, QTRLY COMPARABLE PHARMACY SALES INCREASED 5.4 PERCENT.'}
{'symbol': 'WBA', 'date': '2019-10-28 22:30:00', 'title': 'Walgreens Boots Alliance, Inc. Reports Earnings Results for the Fourth Quarter Ended August 31, 2019', 'text': 'Walgreens Boots Alliance, Inc. announced earnings results for the fourth quarter ended August 31, 2019. For the fourth quarter, the company announced sales was USD 33,954 million compared to USD 33,442 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 878 million compared to USD 1,396 million a year ago. Net income was USD 677 million compared to USD 1,512 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 0.75 compared to USD 1.55 a year ago. For the full year, sales was USD 136,866 million compared to USD 131,537 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 4,998 million compared to USD 6,289 million a year ago. Net income was USD 3,982 million compared to USD 5,024 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 4.32 compared to USD 5.07 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 4.31 compared to USD 5.05 a year ago.'}
